{#
    One borrowed sentence, and the element draws all of it.

    **Every option is a property**, and the sentence is written between the
    tags — the one thing about a quotation an attribute cannot hold, because
    out of a document it carries links and emphasis. Nothing here draws the
    attribution: who said it, what they are to the subject and when are one row
    in one order, and that order is what the component is.
#}
{#- Where a borrowed sentence can be read in full is usually not in this
    manual, so the target is left alone where it points off the site and
    resolved where it points into it — the guard `card` puts on its picture. -#}
{%- set given = node.option('href') -%}
{%- set href = given ? (given is external_target ? given : renderLink(given)) : '' -%}
<sds-quote
    by="{{ node.option('by') }}"
    {%- if node.option('as') %} as="{{ node.option('as') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('meta') %} meta="{{ node.option('meta') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('initials') %} initials="{{ node.option('initials') }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if href %} href="{{ href }}"{% endif %}
    {%- if node.option('class') %} class="{{ node.option('class') }}"{% endif %}
>
    {%- for child in node.children -%}
        {{ renderNode(child) }}
    {%- endfor -%}
</sds-quote>
